1
00:00:00,820 --> 00:00:02,980
Horikita joined the student council,

2
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:06,980
but I haven't gotten any
new information out of her.

3
00:00:07,810 --> 00:00:10,630
Nagumo's personal maneuvering aside,

4
00:00:10,630 --> 00:00:14,070
the management of the student
council appears to be above-board.

5
00:00:15,450 --> 00:00:19,450
The real action started
on a particular weekend,

6
00:00:19,450 --> 00:00:21,870
one week before the deadline
for forming groups.

7
00:00:22,510 --> 00:00:25,740
The vice president, Kiriyama,
had asked to speak with me.

8
00:00:26,590 --> 00:00:27,930
So here we are.

9
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:44,360
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

10
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:54,970
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

11
00:02:00,190 --> 00:02:02,760
How can I help you, Mr. Vice President?

12
00:02:02,990 --> 00:02:05,720
The deserted island test starts
at the end of the month.

13
00:02:04,650 --> 00:02:07,060
#8 The Subject of the Dragons' Gaze

14
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:07,690
Have you completed your preparations?

15
00:02:07,970 --> 00:02:10,430
I've done what I can.

16
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:12,970
What about you, Vice President Kiriyama?

17
00:02:13,470 --> 00:02:18,540
I'm thinking of engaging in an
individual fight in the upcoming test.

18
00:02:18,990 --> 00:02:21,910
An individual fight?

19
00:02:22,150 --> 00:02:26,420
Our class lost the battle with
Nagumo and was dropped down.

20
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:29,700
He's gradually taking control
of the whole school.

21
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:33,320
There's no more fighting our class can do.

22
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:38,550
The only thing I can do is settle
things on an individual basis.

23
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:41,100
I understand.

24
00:02:41,430 --> 00:02:46,220
But I'm not sure why you would
want to tell me about that.

25
00:02:46,220 --> 00:02:49,270
Let's just say I don't want
any outside interference.

26
00:02:49,570 --> 00:02:50,890
Outside interference?

27
00:02:50,890 --> 00:02:53,980
You sent Horikita-senpai's
sister into the student council

28
00:02:53,980 --> 00:02:55,890
to keep an eye on Nagumo, didn't you?

29
00:02:56,230 --> 00:02:59,520
I can't say that wasn't part of it.

30
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:01,910
Though it's not the main reason.

31
00:03:01,910 --> 00:03:05,410
It's so that Horikita can walk
the same path her brother did.

32
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:08,410
You won't get in my way, then?

33
00:03:08,410 --> 00:03:12,040
As long as Horikita doesn't
see Nagumo as an obstacle.

34
00:03:12,260 --> 00:03:13,540
I can't accept that.

35
00:03:13,540 --> 00:03:17,990
Nagumo is aware on some level that I was
leaking information to Horikita-senpai.

36
00:03:17,990 --> 00:03:19,930
Any unwarranted interference now...

37
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:24,680
It could put you in danger?

38
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:27,390
Yes.

39
00:03:28,110 --> 00:03:31,520
Are you looking for a chance
to move up to Class A?

40
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:34,650
What's the point of graduating
in anything but Class A?!

41
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:39,650
I refuse to go down with the
incompetents and weirdos of Class B!

42
00:03:39,990 --> 00:03:41,190
Kiriyama.

43
00:03:46,410 --> 00:03:49,160
You're with an interesting
underclassman, I see.

44
00:03:49,670 --> 00:03:51,790
Ayanokoji Kiyotaka, right?

45
00:03:52,210 --> 00:03:56,290
Spending time with someone like
that won't get you anywhere.

46
00:03:56,290 --> 00:03:58,550
Better than spending time with you.

47
00:03:58,550 --> 00:04:01,420
That's up to Ayanokoji
to decide, I'm sure.

48
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:05,720
That's Kiryuin. She's in Class B with me.

49
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:07,830
I saw her OAA.

50
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:13,560
A highly-regarded student with Academic
Achievement and Physical Ability of A+.

51
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:15,600
She does well on paper.

52
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:18,440
But she doesn't have supporters
like Nagumo does.

53
00:04:18,730 --> 00:04:21,290
She doesn't have a single real friend.

54
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:24,990
Listen to those compliments.
You're making me blush.

55
00:04:25,250 --> 00:04:28,240
Engaging with her is a waste of time.

56
00:04:28,550 --> 00:04:31,620
What's wrong? You won't come to see me?

57
00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:33,120
I think she wants to talk to me.

58
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:36,260
If you don't come to me,
I'll have to come to you.

59
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:37,880
Are you sure you want that?

60
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:42,010
People like her are why I've
had to settle for Class B.

61
00:04:42,530 --> 00:04:46,430
She's a selfish outsider who
doesn't care about anyone else!

62
00:04:46,430 --> 00:04:48,350
Thank you for the compliment.

63
00:04:49,620 --> 00:04:52,350
I'd like to talk to Ayanokoji.

64
00:04:52,350 --> 00:04:53,740
You're in our way.

65
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:58,750
Don't forget what I said.

66
00:04:59,190 --> 00:05:02,490
Watch your step, or I'll
become your enemy, too.

67
00:05:06,790 --> 00:05:09,920
Standing to talk is so
uncivilized. Let's sit.

68
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:10,990
Sure.

69
00:05:13,150 --> 00:05:16,110
So, what did you want to talk to me about?

70
00:05:16,110 --> 00:05:17,420
Anything at all.

71
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:20,750
I just want to get a read on you.

72
00:05:20,990 --> 00:05:22,670
A read on me?

73
00:05:23,020 --> 00:05:26,200
The reason you don't
contribute to your class is

74
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:29,010
because you aren't interested
in your classmates, right?

75
00:05:29,010 --> 00:05:34,390
What I'm not interested in is this
school's system of competing for Class A.

76
00:05:34,870 --> 00:05:38,400
I'm talented enough on my own merits to
get whatever position I want after school.

77
00:05:38,690 --> 00:05:42,400
You wouldn't have come here if
you'd known it was like this, then?

78
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:44,280
Far from it.

79
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:46,970
I like this school.

80
00:05:46,970 --> 00:05:49,870
And the point system affords
me a comfortable life.

81
00:05:50,350 --> 00:05:53,410
You've been asking all the
questions, you know...

82
00:05:53,650 --> 00:05:55,630
Why me, though?

83
00:05:55,630 --> 00:05:58,670
There are lots of students here
with high Academic Achievement.

84
00:05:58,950 --> 00:06:00,420
Instinct.

85
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:04,430
My instinct tells me that
you're extraordinary.

86
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:10,550
Are you going to try to take first
place in the upcoming survival game?

87
00:06:10,550 --> 00:06:14,060
I'm sure every student
wants to take first place.

88
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:17,060
Except people like you, Kiryuin-senpai.

89
00:06:17,350 --> 00:06:21,990
Maybe not first, but I am aiming
for one of the top slots.

90
00:06:21,990 --> 00:06:25,320
A top slot will earn
me more private points.

91
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:28,280
Money tends to burn a hole in my pocket.

92
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:30,570
I never seem to have enough.

93
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:32,830
The upcoming special test

94
00:06:32,830 --> 00:06:35,830
is also a battle to determine
the best student in the school.

95
00:06:36,340 --> 00:06:39,350
Whether or not my interest
in you is misplaced

96
00:06:39,350 --> 00:06:42,210
will be determined by your
achievement on the island.

97
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:47,710
I think I'd rather not have
you interested in me.

98
00:06:47,710 --> 00:06:50,130
You do say the most interesting things.

99
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:53,470
I'm looking forward to fighting you,

100
00:06:53,470 --> 00:06:55,050
Ayanokoji.

101
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:06,740
Well, well. The loyal dog has
returned with its master in tow.

102
00:07:06,740 --> 00:07:07,880
What was that?

103
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:12,610
Hey, don't say hurtful things
to my dear colleague.

104
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:14,950
Dear colleague?

105
00:07:14,950 --> 00:07:17,490
I'm not sure I buy your sincerity.

106
00:07:17,490 --> 00:07:20,250
It's entirely genuine, I assure you.

107
00:07:20,250 --> 00:07:24,290
Now, Mr. President. How can I help you?

108
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:27,670
I didn't think we had any more business.

109
00:07:27,670 --> 00:07:30,510
I certainly don't intend to stay long.

110
00:07:30,510 --> 00:07:33,500
Despite your beauty,
you're entirely lacking in charm.

111
00:07:33,850 --> 00:07:37,260
I have no interest in women like that.

112
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:39,840
Oh, I have a great many charms.

113
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:42,900
I just haven't met the gentleman
who could draw them out of me.

114
00:07:43,190 --> 00:07:47,270
I'd love to see the man who could.

115
00:07:47,270 --> 00:07:49,220
As would I.

116
00:07:49,220 --> 00:07:51,780
I really wonder why the
men aren't all over me.

117
00:07:51,780 --> 00:07:55,780
Men don't know how to
deal with a strong woman.

118
00:07:55,780 --> 00:07:56,870
I see.

119
00:07:57,270 --> 00:08:01,540
If they're all just intimidated,
I completely understand.

120
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:05,290
You've been taking good
care of your hair, I see.

121
00:08:05,810 --> 00:08:07,900
I'm sure the women are all over you.

122
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:11,050
Had any better luck in the romance
department these last three years?

123
00:08:11,270 --> 00:08:16,300
A woman who's never dated a man
wants to comment on my love life?

124
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:19,360
There's no need to be ashamed
of a lack of experience.

125
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:22,810
Couldn't you actually say
it makes me more valuable?

126
00:08:22,810 --> 00:08:26,810
As usual, your mind works
in the strangest ways.

127
00:08:27,140 --> 00:08:29,230
Kiriyama told me what you said.

128
00:08:29,610 --> 00:08:33,590
You've never shown any interest
in me or Horikita-senpai,

129
00:08:33,590 --> 00:08:37,070
yet you've set your sights on
Ayanokoji? Very unexpected.

130
00:08:37,330 --> 00:08:40,150
You seem to be under a misapprehension.

131
00:08:40,150 --> 00:08:43,300
I'm really quite interested in people.

132
00:08:43,300 --> 00:08:46,960
When someone sparks that interest,
I'll happily approach them.

133
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:51,090
You and Horikita Manabu, too... I was
interested in you both at one point.

134
00:08:51,090 --> 00:08:54,090
And what do you make of Ayanokoji?

135
00:08:54,090 --> 00:08:56,060
I'm reserving judgment for now.

136
00:08:56,610 --> 00:09:00,600
I lost interest in you,
but I think he'll be more fun.

137
00:09:00,600 --> 00:09:04,850
You're the only one who could
openly insult me like that.

138
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:08,730
I'd love to rein in that
arrogance of yours.

139
00:09:09,230 --> 00:09:13,890
When you lose, your losses will
be beyond measure, Mr. President.

140
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:16,370
Let's call it aura.

141
00:09:16,370 --> 00:09:21,240
I sensed an aura about him different
from that of you and Horikita Manabu.

142
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:23,370
That's not very concrete.

143
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:26,030
Why not test him, then?

144
00:09:26,030 --> 00:09:28,030
I intend to.

145
00:09:28,030 --> 00:09:33,880
We may see what he can really
do on the upcoming island test.

146
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:38,390
I said I was reserving judgment
on Ayanokoji Kiyotaka earlier...

147
00:09:38,390 --> 00:09:41,290
but I do think he's an
interesting student.

148
00:09:41,290 --> 00:09:42,390
Oh?

149
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:47,270
You see the underclassmen
as amusing playmates.

150
00:09:47,270 --> 00:09:50,400
But if you really went for it,
you'd take first place, no doubt.

151
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:53,730
Oh, there's no question of that.

152
00:09:53,730 --> 00:09:57,900
Either me or my rival Kiriyama.

153
00:09:58,310 --> 00:10:03,290
But if we want to sweep all three top
spots, we'll need another group, won't we?

154
00:10:03,740 --> 00:10:06,650
You should take that role, Kiryuin.

155
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:09,330
I see. So that's what you wanted.

156
00:10:09,770 --> 00:10:13,570
But you have countless other
pawns to call upon, don't you?

157
00:10:13,570 --> 00:10:15,710
You're not interested, then?

158
00:10:15,710 --> 00:10:18,340
So sorry to waste you a trip.

159
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:20,590
I should have expected no less.

160
00:10:20,890 --> 00:10:22,700
It was a waste of time, then.

161
00:10:23,710 --> 00:10:27,980
Since you went to the trouble to come
here, I'll offer you a word of advice.

162
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:31,980
Don't worry about the underclassmen.
Just focus on your path forward.

163
00:10:32,350 --> 00:10:34,730
You may end up burned.

164
00:10:35,380 --> 00:10:37,590
What a ridiculous thing to say.

165
00:10:44,700 --> 00:10:46,860
Off to Keyaki Mall this early?

166
00:10:47,210 --> 00:10:51,250
I won't have time to relax
once the test starts.

167
00:10:51,530 --> 00:10:54,600
Ichinose seems to trust you a lot.

168
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:57,220
Is that trust justified?

169
00:10:57,220 --> 00:11:01,780
We've canceled our alliance,
but I don't view Ichinose as an enemy.

170
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:03,390
Kanzaki...

171
00:11:03,390 --> 00:11:08,280
Are you trying to get some kind of
comment from me to pass on to Ichinose?

172
00:11:09,490 --> 00:11:14,650
You're far sharper than we ever thought.

173
00:11:14,650 --> 00:11:18,900
I can see that Class D's
rapid rise is because of you.

174
00:11:19,270 --> 00:11:20,330
You think so?

175
00:11:21,940 --> 00:11:23,940
I want to ask for your help.

176
00:11:24,250 --> 00:11:27,130
Ichinose trusts you greatly.

177
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:33,130
I want you to tell her that she
needs to change her approach.

178
00:11:33,540 --> 00:11:37,590
You really think that
will get her to change?

179
00:11:38,010 --> 00:11:39,090
Yes.

180
00:11:39,350 --> 00:11:41,700
Sorry, but I can't help you there.

181
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:46,100
I want to see where Ichinose's
approach takes her.

182
00:11:46,830 --> 00:11:52,160
And, fundamentally, it's up
to us to help our own classes.

183
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:53,230
Don't you think?

184
00:11:55,210 --> 00:11:58,480
True. Maybe I'm trying
to defer responsibility.

185
00:11:58,760 --> 00:12:02,490
I feel like I've had the answer I need.

186
00:12:02,490 --> 00:12:08,920
But I'm grasping for alternatives because
I don't want to go through with it.

187
00:12:13,790 --> 00:12:17,390
This is a rather random grouping.

188
00:12:17,390 --> 00:12:20,990
I'd like to know why you called us here.

189
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:23,050
Just relax already.

190
00:12:23,050 --> 00:12:25,140
I couldn't possibly relax.

191
00:12:25,700 --> 00:12:29,560
I don't even want to be
seen in your company.

192
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:33,890
What's Class A's plan in the
deserted island survival game?

193
00:12:33,890 --> 00:12:35,900
What do you mean?

194
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:38,820
Do you have your sights set
merely on class points alone,

195
00:12:38,820 --> 00:12:40,980
or something else?

196
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:43,620
And the fact that Ichinose and Shibata

197
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:47,390
are in a group with Sakayanagi
stinks to high heaven.

198
00:12:47,820 --> 00:12:49,180
Would this be a new alliance?

199
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:52,100
You're free to interpret
it however you like,

200
00:12:52,100 --> 00:12:55,040
but I won't tell you a single thing.

201
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:57,850
Don't be so uptight, Katsuragi.

202
00:12:57,850 --> 00:13:03,550
You'd like it if Sakayanagi got expelled
in the upcoming test, wouldn't you?

203
00:13:03,850 --> 00:13:04,800
What?

204
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:09,390
If she went away,
Class A wouldn't have a leader.

205
00:13:09,390 --> 00:13:12,560
You'd be back on top then.

206
00:13:13,010 --> 00:13:16,690
I don't know what you're
planning, but it won't work.

207
00:13:17,110 --> 00:13:21,190
Sakayanagi has enough points
to save herself from expulsion,

208
00:13:21,410 --> 00:13:23,820
and she can use her
protection point, as well.

209
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:31,220
True, getting her expelled would
require at least two strikes.

210
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:34,800
The idea of doing it in the
next test was a joke, anyway.

211
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:38,330
The deserted island survival game
isn't a place to take down enemies.

212
00:13:38,330 --> 00:13:40,840
It's a place to advance yourself
through your own power.

213
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:45,710
What really matters is that Year 2
doesn't lose any class points.

214
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:49,970
To do that, I need a few allies.

215
00:13:50,410 --> 00:13:53,720
Surely you're not proposing
an alliance with me?

216
00:13:53,990 --> 00:13:55,850
Not just you.

217
00:13:55,850 --> 00:13:58,600
The quiet listener over there, too.

218
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:00,070
Ayanokoji.

219
00:14:00,390 --> 00:14:02,490
Huh? Me, too?

220
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:05,610
You thought I called you
out here for nothing?

221
00:14:06,030 --> 00:14:10,740
He has impressive math skills, but do
you really think he's suitable for this?

222
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:14,410
An understandable concern
from a position of ignorance.

223
00:14:14,410 --> 00:14:17,280
But my strategy is the right call.

224
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:20,630
This man beat me once before, after all.

225
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:23,380
Is that true?

226
00:14:23,380 --> 00:14:26,260
Admit it, Ayanokoji.

227
00:14:26,580 --> 00:14:30,140
Even if I did, do you think
I would work with you?

228
00:14:30,140 --> 00:14:33,890
Not easily, I'm sure.

229
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:37,640
Unbelievable.

230
00:14:38,060 --> 00:14:42,310
I see you weren't serious
about this from the start.

231
00:14:42,310 --> 00:14:44,440
Have you forgotten that,
since last year's island test,

232
00:14:44,440 --> 00:14:47,350
the contract you made with
me has obliged Class A

233
00:14:47,350 --> 00:14:51,030
to send me large numbers
of points every month?

234
00:14:52,910 --> 00:14:55,770
I'm sure that doesn't sit right with you.

235
00:14:55,770 --> 00:14:58,910
But you can't take revenge because
you know it's your fault.

236
00:15:00,790 --> 00:15:03,530
Join Class B, Katsuragi.

237
00:15:04,690 --> 00:15:05,920
Ridiculous.

238
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:08,180
If you don't have the money, I'll pay up.

239
00:15:08,500 --> 00:15:12,160
Even so, you expect me to
abandon the prestige of Class A?

240
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:16,800
I'll be bringing down
Sakayanagi very soon.

241
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:19,810
Once that happens, her class
will enter a downward spiral.

242
00:15:20,330 --> 00:15:21,810
Ryuen Kakeru

243
00:15:20,330 --> 00:15:21,810
Katsuragi Kohei

244
00:15:21,020 --> 00:15:23,220
You remember this, don't you?

245
00:15:23,220 --> 00:15:26,400
The contract we signed last year.

246
00:15:26,740 --> 00:15:27,530
Yes.

247
00:15:27,530 --> 00:15:32,780
I negotiated with Sakayanagi and
let her out of it for five million.

248
00:15:32,780 --> 00:15:35,660
You won't get another chance like this.

249
00:15:36,130 --> 00:15:38,910
Why would you do all of this for me?

250
00:15:38,910 --> 00:15:42,320
You don't think very highly of yourself.

251
00:15:42,320 --> 00:15:46,040
But it's true,
I'm shelling out a lot here.

252
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:50,050
I've already collected the remaining
points needed from my class.

253
00:15:50,050 --> 00:15:52,430
Go on and sign it already.

254
00:15:50,050 --> 00:15:52,430
Class Transfer Contract

255
00:15:50,050 --> 00:15:52,430
July 10th

256
00:15:50,050 --> 00:15:52,430
First Party: Advanced Nurturing High School Class 2-A

257
00:15:50,050 --> 00:15:52,430
Second Party: Advanced Nurturing High School Class 2-B

258
00:15:50,050 --> 00:15:52,430
Ryuen Kakeru

259
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:55,150
You're serious?

260
00:15:55,550 --> 00:15:58,790
See it as fate, and accept it.

261
00:15:59,990 --> 00:16:01,700
What do you expect from me?

262
00:16:02,010 --> 00:16:04,380
Am I allowed to give my opinions freely?

263
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:06,190
Do what you like.

264
00:16:06,490 --> 00:16:10,940
Even your uptight opinions will
be useful from time to time.

265
00:16:11,380 --> 00:16:13,070
By the way, Ayanokoji.

266
00:16:13,580 --> 00:16:15,220
What in the world are you doing?

267
00:16:15,220 --> 00:16:16,020
Oh?

268
00:16:16,550 --> 00:16:21,590
Well... I was wondering how my
coffee would taste if I diluted it

269
00:16:21,590 --> 00:16:23,870
three or four times over.

270
00:16:24,910 --> 00:16:27,460
You're a strange man, Ayanokoji.

271
00:16:30,330 --> 00:16:32,730
What about him, then?

272
00:16:32,730 --> 00:16:37,210
If we let a Class D student into the
group, it will halve our reward.

273
00:16:37,210 --> 00:16:39,910
I didn't say we were
letting him into the group.

274
00:16:40,280 --> 00:16:43,600
I want you to sell us the
Trial card you were dealt.

275
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:45,610
On one condition.

276
00:16:45,930 --> 00:16:52,110
Trade your Halve card for the
Bandwagon card in our class.

277
00:16:52,810 --> 00:16:58,490
If Kei ends up taking a penalty, she can
use Halve to keep it in the safe zone.

278
00:17:00,090 --> 00:17:01,460
It's a deal.

279
00:17:05,660 --> 00:17:08,570
What are you going to do for your group?

280
00:17:08,570 --> 00:17:10,250
The deadline's coming up.

281
00:17:10,250 --> 00:17:14,430
Working alone will let
me be more adaptable.

282
00:17:14,430 --> 00:17:18,600
But if you end up in poor health,
you'll fail on the spot.

283
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:21,260
The penalty is severe.
You'll be expelled.

284
00:17:21,500 --> 00:17:25,270
You haven't formed a group
yet either, have you?

285
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:28,150
You and I have different risk levels.

286
00:17:28,510 --> 00:17:32,650
Last year, you got sick before
the deserted island test.

287
00:17:33,130 --> 00:17:37,410
I think you should form a
group of two for insurance.

288
00:17:37,700 --> 00:17:41,870
But the only two left in the
class are you and Koenji-kun.

289
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:45,510
I have a lead on someone
from another class.

290
00:17:45,910 --> 00:17:49,540
Huh?! You want me to work with Horikita?

291
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,360
Yeah, pretty much.

292
00:17:52,750 --> 00:17:55,720
Her physical abilities are acceptable,

293
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:58,400
but everything else is cause for concern.

294
00:17:58,400 --> 00:18:01,430
Hey, you can't talk to me like that!

295
00:18:01,430 --> 00:18:04,430
Ishizaki, did you know this was
what they were going to ask about?

296
00:18:04,430 --> 00:18:08,770
What's the big deal? No one
else will pair up with you.

297
00:18:08,770 --> 00:18:13,900
But I hate this guy.
And I hate Horikita even more!

298
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:15,770
I won't work with her.

299
00:18:15,770 --> 00:18:19,330
Excuse me. I don't recall
agreeing to work with you.

300
00:18:19,330 --> 00:18:21,780
Huh? What's that supposed to mean?

301
00:18:21,780 --> 00:18:24,530
You're alone because you
were the odd man out.

302
00:18:24,530 --> 00:18:27,600
I was always intending to fight alone.

303
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:30,820
Although we're both alone,
our situations are drastically different.

304
00:18:30,820 --> 00:18:33,500
I wanted to do this alone, too!

305
00:18:33,930 --> 00:18:37,270
Besides, if we're both
singles, that's perfect.

306
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:39,490
Let's compete, Horikita.

307
00:18:39,490 --> 00:18:41,260
May I ask a question?

308
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:44,780
Why are you so opposed to me?

309
00:18:45,170 --> 00:18:49,250
We've had our differences, but I don't
recall giving you a reason for bad blood.

310
00:18:49,560 --> 00:18:52,020
You're the only one who thinks that.

311
00:18:52,460 --> 00:18:54,810
I see this was a waste of time.

312
00:18:54,810 --> 00:18:56,230
Hey, get back here!

313
00:18:56,230 --> 00:18:58,280
Are we competing or not?!

314
00:18:58,530 --> 00:19:01,730
I won't necessarily stick
to a solo strategy.

315
00:19:01,730 --> 00:19:06,090
Once the test starts, I may
join other groups as necessary.

316
00:19:06,430 --> 00:19:07,580
So lame.

317
00:19:07,940 --> 00:19:11,350
The special tests are too important
to worry about appearances.

318
00:19:11,670 --> 00:19:15,960
Even if I join a group,
I hope you'll work hard.

319
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:19,710
If you still beat me,
I'll give you some credit.

320
00:19:21,170 --> 00:19:22,530
Fine by me!

321
00:19:23,340 --> 00:19:25,850
1st Term Closing Ceremony
Schedule
1. Opening speech
2. National anthem
3. Message from acting chairman
4. Speech by student council president
5. School song
6. Closing speech

322
00:19:23,910 --> 00:19:28,910
The end-of-term ceremony
came and passed in a flash.

323
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:35,670
Soon, we'd be heading out for the
deserted island survival test.

324
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:41,490
This won't be your first time
undertaking a special test.

325
00:19:42,270 --> 00:19:47,130
You've spent over a year at this school,
facing and overcoming challenges.

326
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:52,250
But the test you're about to face will
be harsher than any you've faced before.

327
00:19:53,180 --> 00:19:56,500
I'll make just one request of you—

328
00:19:56,940 --> 00:20:03,010
if possible, I want every one of you
back in this classroom when it's over.

329
00:20:04,170 --> 00:20:05,510
Horikita, my girl.

330
00:20:05,780 --> 00:20:07,890
May I talk to you about the test?

331
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:09,830
That's unusual.

332
00:20:09,830 --> 00:20:13,650
Have you decided to voluntarily
participate at last?

333
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:16,300
Let's say you're half right.

334
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:22,900
I know you desperately want the class
points awarded to the top three groups.

335
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:24,160
Naturally.

336
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:26,900
Let's make a deal, then.

337
00:20:26,900 --> 00:20:29,650
If I make a good showing,

338
00:20:29,650 --> 00:20:34,540
will you promise me total freedom
in the class until graduation?

339
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:37,330
That's quite a bold proposal.

340
00:20:37,330 --> 00:20:40,170
You're asking me to indulge your
selfishness moving forward?

341
00:20:40,450 --> 00:20:41,940
Exactly.

342
00:20:41,940 --> 00:20:45,180
Like a full advanced payment
through graduation.

343
00:20:45,550 --> 00:20:48,840
It seems even you're feeling
a sense of desperation.

344
00:20:50,010 --> 00:20:54,550
I'm sorry, but a decent effort
from you isn't worth the trade.

345
00:20:54,550 --> 00:20:57,550
No room to negotiate, then?

346
00:20:57,550 --> 00:21:01,270
No, but I can't accept a vague offer
like "make a good showing."

347
00:21:01,650 --> 00:21:04,340
You must take first place
in the year by yourself.

348
00:21:04,340 --> 00:21:11,150
If you can't, you must promise to work
with us on the next special test.

349
00:21:13,010 --> 00:21:14,790
Yes, very well.

350
00:21:15,110 --> 00:21:17,920
I shall agree to your terms.

351
00:21:18,290 --> 00:21:21,420
You have yourself a deal,
Horikita, my girl.

352
00:21:27,630 --> 00:21:32,900
July's half over already.
It's gotten quite hot.

353
00:21:33,910 --> 00:21:39,020
The doubts over Chairman Sakayanagi's
conduct will also be clearing up soon.

354
00:21:39,020 --> 00:21:42,450
It will become difficult for
me to remain in my position.

355
00:21:43,310 --> 00:21:44,690
All the more reason...

356
00:21:44,690 --> 00:21:48,700
I've prepared a grand
fireworks show for the finale.

357
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:51,640
I'd like you to use any means necessary

358
00:21:51,970 --> 00:21:55,970
to have Ayanokoji Kiyotaka
expelled from the school.

359
00:21:56,920 --> 00:21:58,210
Is that understood?

360
00:21:58,210 --> 00:22:00,680
Yes. I've put my doubts behind me.

361
00:22:02,050 --> 00:22:03,810
I'm counting on you...

362
00:22:05,090 --> 00:22:06,830
Nanase Tsubasa-san.

363
00:22:08,290 --> 00:22:09,030
Yes, sir.
